== 4.7 Chapter 4 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Home trade is trade],
  [within one country],
  [between two countries],
  [in services only],
  [in imports only]
)

#mcq(2, [Home trade is divided into],
  [visible and invisible],
  [entrepot and transit],
  [wholesale and retail],
  [import and export]
)

#mcq(3, [The wholesaler's main customer is],
  [the final consumer],
  [the retailer],
  [the producer],
  [the government]
)

#mcq(4, [Breaking bulk means],
  [insuring goods],
  [increasing the price],
  [dividing large lots into smaller ones],
  [storing goods]
)

#mcq(5, [Which is a function of the wholesaler?],
  [manufacturing goods],
  [grading, packing and storing goods],
  [selling to the final consumer],
  [fixing government prices]
)

#mcq(6, [The wholesaler gives credit mainly to],
  [retailers],
  [the government],
  [banks],
  [consumers]
)

#mcq(7, [A department store is],
  [a self-service grocery],
  [one shop with many departments],
  [many shops with the same goods],
  [a cooperative]
)

#mcq(8, [A multiple shop is],
  [a government shop],
  [one owner with many branches],
  [a market stall],
  [one shop with many departments]
)

#mcq(9, [A supermarket is characterised by],
  [mail order],
  [self-service and a checkout],
  [counter service],
  [credit sales only]
)

#mcq(10, [Selling from a printed catalogue delivered to the buyer is],
  [supermarket trading],
  [hawking],
  [mail order],
  [department store trading]
)

#mcq(11, [Which is an advantage of large-scale retailing?],
  [personal service],
  [quicker decisions],
  [lower prices through bulk buying],
  [less stock]
)

#mcq(12, [Which is a disadvantage of large-scale retailing?],
  [high overheads and slower personal service],
  [a wide range of goods],
  [central buying],
  [lower prices]
)

#mcq(13, [The shortest channel of distribution is],
  [producer to consumer],
  [producer to retailer to consumer],
  [producer to agent to wholesaler to consumer],
  [producer to wholesaler to retailer to consumer]
)

#mcq(14, [Perishable goods usually travel through],
  [the stock exchange],
  [the longest channel],
  [an agent only],
  [the shortest channel]
)

#mcq(15, [Small producers usually use],
  [the shortest channel],
  [no channel at all],
  [a long channel through wholesalers],
  [direct export]
)

#mcq(16, [A middleman is best described as],
  [a producer],
  [a consumer],
  [a link between producer and consumer],
  [a regulator]
)

#mcq(17, [Cutting out the middleman normally],
  [returns his functions to producer or retailer],
  [removes his functions],
  [has no effect on price],
  [reduces the need for storage]
)

#mcq(18, [Trade discount is],
  [a reduction for prompt payment],
  [a reduction off the list price],
  [a penalty],
  [a tax]
)

#mcq(19, [Cash discount is allowed for],
  [advertising],
  [buying in bulk],
  [returning goods],
  [paying within a stated period]
)

#mcq(20, [A trader buys at ₦2,000 and sells at ₦2,500. His mark-up is],
  [50%],
  [125%],
  [25%],
  [20%]
)

#mcq(21, [Using the same figures, the margin is],
  [25%],
  [80%],
  [50%],
  [20%]
)

#mcq(22, [Goods listed at ₦10,000 less 10% trade discount cost],
  [₦9,000],
  [₦8,000],
  [₦11,000],
  [₦9,500]
)

#mcq(23, [An invoice of ₦9,000 less 5% cash discount is settled by],
  [₦8,500],
  [₦8,550],
  [₦8,600],
  [₦9,450]
)

#mcq(24, [Which retail type sells food and household goods by self-service?],
  [department store],
  [mail order house],
  [multiple shop],
  [supermarket]
)

#mcq(25, [A cooperative store sells mainly to],
  [retailers],
  [the public at large],
  [the government],
  [its members]
)

#mcq(26, [The chain of distribution ends with the],
  [wholesaler],
  [consumer],
  [producer],
  [retailer]
)

#mcq(27, [Which function does the retailer perform that the wholesaler does not?],
  [selling to the final consumer],
  [storing goods],
  [transporting goods],
  [breaking bulk]
)

#mcq(28, [A hypermarket differs from a supermarket in that it],
  [is owned by government],
  [is larger and sells a wider range],
  [sells only food],
  [does not use checkouts]
)

#mcq(29, [Which is a reason for the growth of large-scale retailing?],
  [higher prices],
  [higher personal service],
  [smaller stocks],
  [bulk buying and advertising economies]
)

#mcq(30, [A hawker is a],
  [cooperative],
  [producer],
  [mobile retailer],
  [wholesaler]
)

#mcq(31, [Which pair is correctly matched?],
  [mail order: counter service],
  [supermarket: self-service, food-led],
  [department store: many buildings, one department],
  [multiple shop: one building, many departments]
)

#mcq(32, [The wholesaler advises the producer on],
  [the tax rate],
  [the law],
  [what is selling and what is not],
  [the exchange rate]
)

#mcq(33, [Risk-bearing by the wholesaler refers to],
  [the risk of bad debts only],
  [insuring the goods],
  [the risk of theft only],
  [the risk of unsold stock and falling prices]
)

#mcq(34, [A retailer who buys direct from the manufacturer will usually],
  [pay more per unit and carry less stock],
  [sell fewer goods],
  [avoid all storage],
  [pay less per unit and carry more stock]
)

#mcq(35, [Which is NOT a channel of distribution?],
  [producer to consumer],
  [producer to retailer to consumer],
  [consumer to producer to wholesaler],
  [producer to wholesaler to retailer to consumer]
)

#mcq(36, [Agents are most common in],
  [imports and agricultural produce],
  [supermarkets],
  [retail grocery],
  [department stores]
)

#mcq(37, [The main benefit of the channel chosen is measured by],
  [the total cost and service delivered to the buyer],
  [the producer's profit alone],
  [the size of the shops],
  [the number of links]
)

#mcq(38, [A multiple shop buys],
  [centrally for all branches],
  [each branch separately],
  [from government],
  [from consumers]
)

#mcq(39, [Goods sold on credit to a consumer are a function of],
  [the bank],
  [the retailer],
  [the producer],
  [the wholesaler]
)

#mcq(40, [The final link in the chain adds],
  [possession utility only],
  [no utility at all],
  [place and time utility through display and availability],
  [form utility]
)

