  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The national frontier is the boundary that defines it.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The division follows the customer: retailer to consumer, wholesaler to retailer.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    That is what separates him from the retailer.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The wholesaler divides the producer's lot into lots a retailer can buy.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The wholesaler grades, packs, stores and delivers in retailer-sized lots.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Credit flows down the chain, from wholesaler to retailer and retailer to consumer.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Many departments under one roof and one management.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Central buying, standard display, one name across many towns.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Self-service and a single exit checkout are its defining features.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Mail order sells before it stocks, which is the same principle as e-commerce.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Bulk buying lowers unit cost, part of which is passed to the customer.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Rent, staff and stock all rise with scale.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Direct selling removes every middleman.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The shorter the channel, the less time the good spends in transit.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Wholesalers collect from many small producers, which no single producer could afford.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    He performs functions that would otherwise fall on the parties on either side.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The functions survive even when the person performing them changes.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    It fixes the invoice price and is never recorded in the ledger.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    It is an inducement to early payment and is recorded in the books.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Mark-up is profit over cost: 500 ÷ 2,000 = 25%.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The margin is profit over selling price: 500 ÷ 2,500 = 20%.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    10% of 10,000 is 1,000, so the invoice is 9,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    5% of 9,000 is 450, so the payment is 8,550.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Self-service with a checkout is the supermarket.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The benefit is reserved for members, who own the store.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The final buyer is the end of the chain.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Both break bulk and store; only the retailer faces the consumer.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    It adds clothing, electronics and household goods to the food floor.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Scale lowers buying and promotional cost per unit.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    He takes the goods to the buyer rather than waiting for the buyer to come.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Self-service and food are the supermarket's marks.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    His position in the chain gives him daily information about demand.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    He owns the stock while he holds it, so he carries its commercial risk.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The wholesaler's margin is saved, but his functions must be taken on.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Goods move toward the consumer, not away from him.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Agents sell on behalf of distant principals who need local representation.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    A channel is efficient when it delivers the service at the lowest total cost.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Central buying is what gives the chain its cost advantage.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Consumer credit is offered at the point of sale, by the retailer.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The retailer puts the good where and when the consumer wants it.
  ]

]

